    authorLine: 'Author: Onur Aksoy (Hackonomist) · Publisher: Onur Aksoy',
    editorialP1:
      'As the digital sphere shifts from search engines to answer engines, moving from indexed hyperlinks to probabilistic weights, digital identity faces a quiet crisis. In an age of infinite automated output, generative systems do not understand individuals and organizations with greater fidelity; instead, they dilute identities within "name twins" and homonym collisions, flattening distinct legacies into statistical averages.',
    editorialP2:
      'This monograph investigates the reality of digital invisibility hiding behind the fear of surveillance, the modern renaissance of institutional seals and verified records, and the foundational architectural strategy required to build an enduring semantic footprint that resists erasure in the hazy memory of neural networks.',
